    "result_text": "The change is complete and the test suite passes (`BUILD SUCCESS`, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`).\n\n## Summary\n\nI moved all date-derived owner values to a **fiscal-year basis** (fiscal year starts 1 July, named by the calendar year it ends in \u2014 the Australian convention matching this app's holidays/timezones). Every value is derived from the owner's already business-day-adjusted `registrationDate` (set in `BuildOwner`).\n\n**New code**\n- `FiscalYear.java` \u2014 `of(date)` returns the fiscal year (year+1 for dates on/after 1 July, else year); `label(date)` returns the `FY<YY>` string (null-safe).\n\n**Changed behaviour**\n- **New `fiscalYear` response field** \u2014 added to the `Owner` schema in `openapi.yml` (so the generated `OwnerDto` exposes it) and wired in `OwnerMapper` to `FiscalYear.label(...)`, yielding e.g. `FY27`.\n- **Membership identifier year segment** \u2014 `MembershipNumber` now uses `FiscalYear.of(...) % 100` instead of the calendar year, so a July-2026 registration reads `...-M27`.\n- **Tenure** \u2014 `MembershipPoints` now grants its +3 when at least one fiscal year has elapsed (`FiscalYear.of(now) - FiscalYear.of(registrationDate) >= 1`) rather than a 365-day window. A newly created owner shares the current fiscal year, so it still earns no tenure points.\n\nI also updated the surrounding docs to match: the OpenAPI descriptions/examples for `membershipNumber` and `membershipPoints`, plus the javadoc on `MembershipNumber`, `MembershipPoints`, and `MembershipLevel`.\n\nThe audit log from the run confirms the end-to-end result: `membershipNumber=NSW-16E6609E-M27` for a `2026-09-08` registration, and the acceptance test's `fiscalYear` (`FY27`) matches the required `FY\\d{2}` format.\n\nOne judgment call worth flagging: the spec fixes the format (`FY<YY>`) and start date (1 July) but not whether the label is the fiscal year's *start* or *end* year. I chose the end-year (Australian) convention; the one acceptance test only checks the format, so if you intended start-year (which would give `FY26`/`M26` here) it's a one-line change in `FiscalYear.of`.",
